            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral inguinal hernia with an uncommon content : A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-496</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Here we present a sixty-two year old man with bilateral swellings palpated in inguinal areas on physical examination. Ultrasonography and abdominal multi-detector computed tomography revealed a bladder herniation through the right inguinal canal and a sigmoid colon herniation through the left inguinal canal. Radiologic imaging methods are important and can guide clinicians for preemptive or emergent surgery. (Acta gastroenterol. belg., 2016, 79, 495-496).</AbstractText>
